{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.NonsingularInverse","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.PosDef","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Symmetric","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Shared.DetFin","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3GramNondegeneracy"],"declarations":41,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_det_eq_zero_via_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_det_eq_zero_via_general","kind":"theorem","line":748,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L748-L757","doc":"**The D-frame determinant, reached through the general form.**\n\n`gramMatrixD_det_eq_zero` proves this from the explicit radical, which is the\nmore informative route -- it hands back the null direction. Stating it here as a\nfact about `QOU.Machinery.H3.gramMatrix` is what makes the agreement between the\nhand-written table and the general form a proof rather than a coincidence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_eq_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_eq_general","kind":"theorem","line":740,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L740-L746","doc":"**Convention C is the general Gram at `z = u/(u²+1)`**, with `u = √q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_eq_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_eq_general","kind":"theorem","line":731,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L731-L737","doc":"**Convention D is the general Gram at `z = q³/(q²+1)`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_not_posDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_not_posDef","kind":"theorem","line":698,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L698-L711","doc":"**THEOREM.** The canonical Gram is not positive definite, for any `q`.\n\nThis retracts, in the canonical frame, the positive-definiteness reading\nthat the C-frame positivity chain (`detFactor1_pos` … `detFactor6_pos`)\nsupports. Note what the proof does *not* need: no spectrum, no `q > 1`,\nno substrate anchor — a single non-zero vector in the radical settles it.\nAt `q₀` the D-frame spectrum is in fact indefinite (one zero AND one\nnegative eigenvalue), which is strictly worse than this theorem says. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_det_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_det_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":686,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L686-L696","doc":"**THEOREM.** `det G_D(q) = 0` for every real `q`.\n\nThe canonical counterpart of `gramMatrix_det_ne_zero`, and its negation\nin substance: that theorem is true in convention C, this one in D, and D\nis the canonical frame. Proved from the explicit radical via\n`Matrix.exists_mulVec_eq_zero_iff` — which also means the proof *hands\nback* the null direction rather than merely asserting the determinant\nvanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_mulVec_radical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_mulVec_radical","kind":"theorem","line":674,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L674-L684","doc":"**THEOREM.** The q-antisymmetriser is annihilated by the canonical Gram:\n`G_D(q) *ᵥ v = 0`, for every real `q` — no positivity, no `q ≠ 0`, no\nsubstrate hypothesis. Six row identities, each closed by clearing the\n`(q²+1)` denominators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramRadicalD_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramRadicalD_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":666,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L666-L671","doc":"**THEOREM.** The radical direction is non-zero — its last coordinate is\n`1`, for every `q`, including `q = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramRadicalD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramRadicalD","kind":"def","line":655,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L655-L664","doc":"The radical direction: `(−q³, q², q², −q, −q, 1)`, which is\n`−q³ · Σ_w (−1/q)^ℓ(w) T_w` — the three-strand q-antisymmetriser in the\nGröbner–Shirshov normal-form basis `[1, σ₀, σ₁, σ₀σ₁, σ₁σ₀, σ₀σ₁σ₀]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_top_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_top_left","kind":"theorem","line":652,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L652-L653","doc":"**THEOREM.** `G[0,0] = tr_M(1) = 1`. Also unchanged from C. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_isSymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_isSymm","kind":"theorem","line":646,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L646-L650","doc":"**THEOREM.** The canonical Gram matrix is symmetric. Unchanged from C:\n`tr_M(ab) = tr_M(ba)` holds for every Markov weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramEntryD_zero_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramEntryD_zero_one","kind":"theorem","line":639,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L639-L644","doc":"**THEOREM.** The `(0,1)` entry IS the Markov weight, `G[0,1] = tr_M(σ₀) = z`.\n\nA one-line convention anchor: it pins, in checkable Lean rather than in a\ndocstring, which `z` these entries were built from. The corresponding\nC-frame entry is `gramEntry u 0 1 = u/(u²+1) = √q/(q+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD","kind":"def","line":635,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L635-L637","doc":"The canonical (convention-D) H_3(q) Gram matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramEntryD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramEntryD","kind":"def","line":593,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L593-L633","doc":"The 36 Gram entries on the H_3(q) NF basis in **convention D**, as\nrational functions of `q`. Every denominator is a power of `q² + 1`,\nwhich is positive over `ℝ` for every `q` — so unlike the C entries these\nneed no `q ≠ 0` side condition anywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.markovWeightD_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.markovWeightD_root","kind":"theorem","line":580,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L580-L591","doc":"**THEOREM.** `z_D` is a root of the determinant factor `(q²+1)z − q³`.\n\nThis is the whole reason the canonical Gram is singular, recorded in Lean\nrather than only in prose: the generic determinant over `ℚ(q,z)` carries\n`(q²+1)z − q³` as a factor, and `markovWeightD` annihilates it for every\n`q`. Stating it here means a later edit cannot quietly relabel this file\nto D and leave a false non-singularity claim standing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.markovWeightD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.markovWeightD","kind":"def","line":577,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L577-L578","doc":"The canonical Markov weight, **convention D**: `z = q³/(q² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_det_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_det_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":526,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L526-L538","doc":"**THEOREM (convention C only — FALSE in the canonical convention D).**\nCombines the conditional discharge (above) with the symbolic\nfactorization theorem to give `u > 1 ⟹ det(G_C(u)) ≠ 0`.\n\nStatus: FULLY PROVED (sorry-free) — and scoped. The proof is sound; the\n*frame* is not canonical. Convention D is a root of the determinant\nfactor `(q²+1)z − q³`, so the D-frame Gram is singular for every `q`\n(`gramMatrixD_det_eq_zero`). Cite this as a C-frame result, never as\n\"the H_3 Gram is non-singular\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_det_eq_factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_det_eq_factorization","kind":"theorem","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L508-L524","doc":"**THEOREM (PROVED).** The symbolic `Matrix.det` of `gramMatrix u` equals\nthe witness-derived factorization, for every real `u`. The 6×6 determinant\nis expanded via `det_fin_six` on the denominator-cleared polynomial matrix\n`gramScaled` (`gramScaled_det`), related back to `gramMatrix` by the row\nscaling `gram_scale_rel` and `∏ Lval = u¹⁸(u²+1)¹²`. The `u = 0` boundary\n(where both sides are `0` under Lean's `x / 0 = 0`) is discharged directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gram_det_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gram_det_eq","kind":"theorem","line":489,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L489-L504","doc":"Symbolic factorization of `det(gramMatrix u)` for `u ≠ 0`, obtained from\n`gramScaled_det` by dividing out the row scales `∏ Lval = u¹⁸(u²+1)¹²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gram_scale_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gram_scale_rel","kind":"theorem","line":476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L476-L485","doc":"The scaled matrix equals `diagonal (Lval u) * gramMatrix u` (entrywise,\nafter clearing denominators; needs `u ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramScaled_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramScaled_det","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L465-L472","doc":"Determinant of the polynomial scaled Gram matrix, by direct\n`det_fin_six` expansion + `ring` (no division — all entries polynomial). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramScaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramScaled","kind":"def","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L460-L461","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramScaledEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramScaledEntry","kind":"def","line":420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L420-L458","doc":"Polynomial (denominator-cleared) Gram matrix `= diagonal (Lval u) * gramMatrix u`.\nVerified entrywise in `gram_scale_rel`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.Lval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.Lval","kind":"def","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L410-L418","doc":"Row-scale factors `L_i`; `diagonal L * gram` clears all denominators\n(turning each rational Gram entry into a polynomial). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_det_ne_zero_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_det_ne_zero_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L364-L408","doc":"**THEOREM (det ≠ 0 conditional on symbolic factorization).** If the\nsymbolic Matrix.det of `gramMatrix u` equals the witness's\nfactorization, then it is non-zero for `u > 1`.\n\nThe factorization equality itself (`gramMatrix u . det = -(numerator)/(denominator)`)\nis recorded in `gram-h3-det-factorization.witness.json` as a sympy-\nverified identity; the full Lean expansion of `Matrix.det` for the\n6×6 rational-function matrix is multi-thousand-line work scoped as\na separate follow-up. The conditional discharge below is the\nsubstantive content: the 6 positivity lemmas + denominator\npositivity give a complete categorical argument modulo the\nsympy-witnessed factorization identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gram_det_denominator_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gram_det_denominator_pos","kind":"theorem","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L357-L362","doc":"**POSITIVITY LEMMA (denominator).** `u^10 · (u² + 1)^12 > 0` for `u > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor6_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor6_pos","kind":"theorem","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L345-L355","doc":"**POSITIVITY LEMMA 6.** `r(u) = u⁶ + u⁵ + 2u⁴ + u³ + u² + u + 1 > 0`\nfor `u > 0` (all coefficients positive). Trivially `> 7` for `u > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor5_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor5_pos","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L323-L343","doc":"**POSITIVITY LEMMA 5.** `p(u) = u⁶ − u⁵ + u⁴ − u³ + 2u² − u + 1 > 0`\n  for `u > 1`. Strategy: group as `(u−1)(u⁵ + u³) + (2u² − u + 1)` where\n-- Witness: computations/none\n  the first part is positive (product of positives for `u > 1`) and the\n  second has discriminant `1 − 8 = −7 < 0`, so is always positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor4_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor4_pos","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L314-L321","doc":"**POSITIVITY LEMMA 4.** `u³ + u² + 1 > 0` for `u > 1`\n(every term `> 0` when `u > 0`; trivially `> 3` when `u > 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L302-L312","doc":"**POSITIVITY LEMMA 3.** `u³ + u − 1 > 0` for `u > 1`. At `u = 1`:\n`1 + 1 − 1 = 1 > 0`; for `u > 1`, `u³ > 0` and `u − 1 > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor2_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor2_pos","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L298-L300","doc":"**POSITIVITY LEMMA 2.** `u + 1 > 0` for `u > 1` (trivially `> 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor1_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor1_pos","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L294-L296","doc":"**POSITIVITY LEMMA 1.** `u − 1 > 0` for `u > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor6","kind":"def","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L289-L292","doc":"Factor 6: r(u) = u⁶ + u⁵ + 2u⁴ + u³ + u² + u + 1\n(all-positive coefficients). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor5","kind":"def","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L285-L287","doc":"Factor 5: p(u) = u⁶ − u⁵ + u⁴ − u³ + 2u² − u + 1 (no real roots). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor4","kind":"def","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L282-L283","doc":"Factor 4: u³ + u² + 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor3","kind":"def","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L279-L280","doc":"Factor 3: u³ + u − 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor2","kind":"def","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L276-L277","doc":"Factor 2: u + 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.detFactor1","kind":"def","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L273-L274","doc":"Factor 1: u − 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_top_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_top_left","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L207-L210","doc":"**THEOREM.** The top-left Gram entry is `1 = tr_M(1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_isSymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix_isSymm","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L197-L205","doc":"**THEOREM.** The Gram matrix is symmetric:\n`G[i,j] = G[j,i]` for all `i, j ∈ Fin 6`.\n\nProved by direct case analysis on the 36 pairs; each cell-equality\nis `rfl` after `unfold gramEntry` because we encoded the entries\nexplicitly symmetrically. Numerically verified at q_0 to ≤ 1e-16. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrix","kind":"def","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L191-L193","doc":"The H_3(q) Gram matrix as a Mathlib `Matrix`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:gram-matrix-h3-symbolic","label":"prop:gram-matrix-h3-symbolic","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-matrix-h3-symbolic.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramEntry","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramMatrixH3Symbolic.lean#L143-L189","doc":"The 21 upper-triangle Gram entries on the H_3(q) NF basis **in\nconvention C** (`z = √q/(q+1)`, excised 2026-08-09 / re-affirmed\n2026-08-15), in terms of `u = √q` (so `q = u²` is the Hecke parameter).\nThe entries are Laurent polynomials in `u` (cleanly factored).\n\nThe `u = √q` parametrisation is forced by C and by nothing else: C's `z`\nis irrational in `q`, so odd powers of `u` appear. The canonical\n`gramEntryD` below is rational in `q` and needs no square root — see\nthe file banner. ","signatureChunk":0}]}